  "summary": "An AP article reports that Flock's ALPR cameras have become a bipartisan campaign issue in the 2026 midterms, with candidates in Wisconsin, Pennsylvania, Texas, Michigan, Rhode Island, and Florida proposing bans, funding cuts, or restrictions. It contrasts these positions with law enforcement groups and Flock's defense of the technology, and notes recent actions like Florida removing ALPRs from state highways and Rhode Island's governor pausing installations.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "candidates from both parties are increasingly on the attack over Flock cameras, the AI-powered nationwide network of automated cameras that record license plates",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock cameras are an intrusive invasion of privacy and they should be banned.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "outgoing Republican Gov. Ron DeSantis's administration this week ordered the removal of automated license plate readers from state highway rights-of-way",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
